* ''No backward compatibility in early alpha'' (operator, 2026-11-07: //"'no backward compatability needed in early alpha' remains house law."//). A rename, a re-key or a shape change carries no record across it, and every CRDT doc re-genesises until the founding bake (`X0`); the registry's domain renames re-key their records under this law.

